articles.content_en:
Article 1 An Internet Court shall have centralized jurisdiction over the following first-instance cases that shall be accepted by Primary People's Courts within the city's jurisdiction:
(1) disputes over ownership, infringement and contract of network data;
(2) disputes over network personal information protection and privacy rights;
(3) disputes over ownership, infringement and contract of network virtual property;
(4) disputes over network unfair competition;
(5) disputes over ownership, infringement and contract of network domain names;
(6) disputes arising from entering into or performing online shopping contracts through e-commerce platforms;
(7) disputes over network service contracts where the acts of entering into and performing the contract are both completed online;
(8) administrative disputes arising from administrative actions such as network data supervision, network personal information protection supervision, network unfair competition supervision, network transaction management, and network information service management taken by administrative organs; and
(9) cases of network public interest litigation initiated by procuratorial organs.
Foreign-related civil cases and civil cases involving the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region, the Macao Special Administrative Region, and the Taiwan region that meet the provisions of the preceding paragraph shall be under the jurisdiction of the Internet Court.
Upon approval by the Supreme People's Court, the relevant Higher People's Court may designate the Internet Court to have jurisdiction over other specific types of network civil and administrative cases.
